comment.narrative:
To date, 502,853 hectares of land are under sustainable land management practices, mainly through conservation area development activities in 54 communes (fencing and reforestation of degraded areas, establishment of COGES, construction of firebreaks, etc.); this represents 50% of the final target achieved.

As part of the restructuring, the final target for this indicator will be revised downward to 700,000 hectares for the following main reasons:

- A downward trend in the size of conservation areas;
- A reduction in the number of parks to be certified, from 250 to 48;
- The abandonment of high forest-potential areas in Gulmou and NakambE for security reasons.

The new target value will be estimated taking into account the contribution of the new activities proposed under the project restructuring (agro-sylvo-pastoral developments and landscape developments) and will be replaced by the World Bank scorecard indicator on terrestrial land under improved management/conservation.

